Targets: wasm
Subject: Walk the plan with a walker of the signature the walker interface calls
Purpose: In the first minor releases of 10, ExecShutdownNode(PlanState *) hands itself to planstate_tree_walker(), which calls its walker as walker(node, context) through a pointer declared with an empty parameter list. Native code tolerates the extra argument; WebAssembly traps on a call through a pointer whose signature differs from the function's ("null function or function signature mismatch"), which stopped every query at the end of ExecutorRun. The wrapper has the exact shape the walker is called with. Later minors do this themselves (ExecShutdownNode_walker); the series lists this patch as optional ("|-") and scripts/patches.js refuses to skip it while the text it changes is still there.
Components: src/backend/executor/execProcnode.c
Checks: scripts/build-wasm.sh creates the template data directory and the node and browser tests pass for the first minor of 10
Origin: own

diff --git a/src/backend/executor/execProcnode.c b/src/backend/executor/execProcnode.c
--- a/src/backend/executor/execProcnode.c
+++ b/src/backend/executor/execProcnode.c
@@ -718,6 +718,17 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * planstate_tree_walker() calls its walker as walker(node, context).  A walker of that shape is needed here because
+ * WebAssembly traps a call through a function pointer whose signature differs from the function's own (ExecShutdownNode
+ * takes one argument), which native code tolerates.
+ */
+static bool
+ExecShutdownNodeWalker(PlanState *node, void *context)
+{
+	return ExecShutdownNode(node);
+}
+
+/*
  * ExecShutdownNode
  *
  * Give execution nodes a chance to stop asynchronous resource consumption
@@ -735,7 +746,7 @@
 
 	check_stack_depth();
 
-	planstate_tree_walker(node, ExecShutdownNode, NULL);
+	planstate_tree_walker(node, ExecShutdownNodeWalker, NULL);
 
 	switch (nodeTag(node))
 	{
